      "srt": "1\n00:00:0,000 --> 00:00:4,600\nAnd remember, you've seen this episode\n\n2\n00:00:1,790 --> 00:00:4,600\n \n\n3\n00:00:1,800 --> 00:00:7,160\nbefore. Here's how it typically goes.\n\n4\n00:00:4,590 --> 00:00:7,160\n \n\n5\n00:00:4,600 --> 00:00:8,800\nStep one, the company decides it's time\n\n6\n00:00:7,150 --> 00:00:8,800\n \n\n7\n00:00:7,160 --> 00:00:11,120\nto cut costs.\n\n8\n00:00:8,790 --> 00:00:11,120\n \n\n9\n00:00:8,800 --> 00:00:12,800\nAnd what's the easiest way to do that?\n\n10\n00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:12,800\n \n\n11\n00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:14,560\nFire the monkeys.\n\n12\n00:00:12,790 --> 00:00:14,560\n \n\n13\n00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,880\nWow, genius-level business management at\n\n14\n00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:16,880\n \n\n15\n00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:19,240\nplay here, folks. Just give everything\n\n16\n00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:19,240\n \n\n17\n00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:20,760\nto chat GPT, Claude, and Copilot, and\n\n18\n00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:20,760\n \n\n19\n00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:23,600\nthey'll do the rest.\n\n20\n00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:23,600\n \n\n21\n00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:26,480\nSee, in the first quarter of 2026 alone,\n\n22\n00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:26,480\n \n\n23\n00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:27,920\nnearly 80,000 tech jobs got cut.\n\n24\n00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:27,920\n \n\n25\n00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,800\nAnd about half of those were blamed\n\n26\n00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:29,800\n \n\n27\n00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:32,119\ndirectly on AI.\n\n28\n00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:32,119\n \n\n29\n00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:35,080\nStandard Chartered alone announced 7,000\n\n30\n00:00:32,109 --> 00:00:35,080\n \n\n31\n00:00:32,119 --> 00:00:36,720\njobs gone, betting big on automation.\n\n32\n00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:36,720\n \n\n33\n00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:39,080\nMeta, Amazon, and many others have\n\n34\n00:00:36,710 --> 00:00:39,080\n \n\n35\n00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:40,640\nfollowed suit. But who cares?\n\n36\n00:00:39,070 --> 00:00:40,640\n \n\n37\n00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:42,240\nWe're out here maximizing shareholder\n\n38\n00:00:40,630 --> 00:00:42,240\n \n\n39\n00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:46,320\nvalue, right?\n\n40\n00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:46,320\n \n\n41\n00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:47,920\nSo, job's done. The monkeys are gone.\n\n42\n00:00:46,310 --> 00:00:47,920\n \n\n43\n00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:50,880\nSurely the AI agents will do the job\n\n44\n00:00:47,910 --> 00:00:50,880\n \n\n45\n00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:52,160\nproperly, right? Except, this has failed\n\n46\n00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:52,160\n \n\n47\n00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:55,400\nrepeatedly\n\n48\n00:00:52,150 --> 00:00:55,400\n \n\n49\n00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:56,880\nacross many, many industries.\n\n50\n00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:56,880\n \n\n51\n00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:59,000\nVolkswagen poured a fortune into\n\n52\n00:00:56,870 --> 00:00:59,000\n \n\n53\n00:00:56,880 --> 00:01:1,320\nbuilding one unified AI operating system\n\n54\n00:00:58,990 --> 00:01:1,320\n \n\n55\n00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:3,840\nfor every single brand they own.\n\n56\n00:01:1,310 --> 00:01:3,840\n \n\n57\n00:01:1,320 --> 00:01:6,000\nThe result? A 20 million-line mess\n\n58\n00:01:3,830 --> 00:01:6,000\n \n\n59\n00:01:3,840 --> 00:01:8,960\nriddled with bugs. The Porsche electric\n\n60\n00:01:5,990 --> 00:01:8,960\n \n\n61\n00:01:6,000 --> 00:01:13,000\nand Audi Q6 e-tron delayed over a year,\n\n62\n00:01:8,950 --> 00:01:13,000\n \n\n63\n00:01:8,960 --> 00:01:13,000\nand 1,600 jobs cut.\n\n"
